# CoW 2G — String.push_char builtin drift. The prescan's hand-written
# MUTATING_METHODS list had drifted from the typed builtin registry, missing
# real is_mutating builtins (add, close, get_or_put, push_char, push_line, send,
# set_at, store, update). Routing the mutating check through the typed
# `is_mutating_builtin_method` predicate picks these up for free, so a bare
# String param mutated with `push_char` in a loop gets the loop-carried
# materialize. Expect the private copy grows to 5 (2 + 3), caller stays 2.
#
# In known_gaps/ (out of the runtime-diff corpus) because push_char is OUTSIDE
# the ggdef phase-0 subset (Core #9 subset gap, filed in TODO). Rust lane is
# correct.
void g(String s):
    int i = 0
    while i < 3:
        s.push_char('x')
        i = i + 1
    print(s.len())

void main():
    String t = "ab"
    g(t)
    print(t.len())
